CAT = "ea2Partnerships"; SEG = "PTR"
# Partnerships: formation, dealings, basis, dispositions, filing, centralized audit regime.
Q = [
("A partnership pays commissions to a broker to sell interests to new investors. Under section 709 these syndication costs are:",
 "Capitalized with no write-off", ["Capitalized, amortized over 180 months", "Deducted up to $5,000, rest amortized", "Deducted in full when paid"],
 "Section 709(a) denies any deduction for amounts paid to promote or sell partnership interests, and the 709(b) election to deduct and amortize covers only organizational expenses, not syndication costs."),
("A limited partner who performs no services receives only a distributive share of ordinary income. For self-employment tax, that share is:",
 "Not self-employment income", ["Fully self-employment income", "Self-employment income if over $400", "Half self-employment income"],
 "Section 1402(a)(13) excludes a limited partner's distributive share from net earnings from self-employment. Only guaranteed payments for services actually rendered are included for a limited partner."),
("A guaranteed payment a calendar-year partner receives from a fiscal-year partnership is included in the partner's income:",
 "For the year the partnership year ends", ["When the cash is actually received", "When the payment agreement is signed", "Ratably over the payment's term"],
 "Section 706(a) bases a partner's inclusions under sections 702 and 707(c) on the partnership year ending within or with the partner's year, so a guaranteed payment is reported with that year's K-1, not when paid."),
("A 70% partner sells equipment to the partnership at a gain, and the partnership will depreciate it in its business. The partner's gain is:",
 "Ordinary income", ["Section 1231 gain", "Long-term capital gain", "Not recognized at all"],
 "Section 707(b)(2) makes gain ordinary on a sale between a partnership and a more-than-50% partner of property that is not a capital asset in the buyer's hands, such as depreciable business equipment."),
("A domestic partnership must file Form 1065 for any tax year in which it:",
 "Had income or deductions", ["Had net taxable income", "Had more than $600 of income", "Made cash distributions"],
 "The Form 1065 instructions require a return from every domestic partnership unless it neither receives income nor incurs expenditures treated as deductions or credits. A loss year still needs a return."),
("An eligible partnership elects out of the centralized audit regime by:",
 "Filing Schedule B-2 with a timely return", ["Filing Form 8832 at any time", "Filing Form 7004 before the return", "Filing Form 8082 after an audit"],
 "Section 6221(b) requires the election on a timely filed return for that year, made on Schedule B-2 (Form 1065) with each partner's name and TIN, and the partners must be notified within 30 days."),
("Form 7004 gives a partnership an automatic extension to file Form 1065 of:",
 "6 months", ["5 months", "3 months", "4 months"],
 "A timely Form 7004 extends a partnership's filing deadline by 6 months, to the 15th day of the 9th month for a calendar-year partnership. It does not extend time for partners to report their own taxes."),
("The penalty for filing Form 1065 late without reasonable cause is figured for:",
 "Each partner for each month late", ["Each month on the unpaid tax", "Each partner once per year", "The return as one flat amount"],
 "Section 6698 imposes a penalty per month or part of a month, up to 12 months, multiplied by the number of persons who were partners at any time during the year. A partnership owes no income tax to base it on."),
("Each partner must receive a Schedule K-1 (Form 1065) by:",
 "The 1065 due date with extensions", ["January 31 of the next year", "April 15 of the next year", "60 days after the year ends"],
 "Section 6031(b) requires the partnership to furnish each partner's K-1 on or before the day the return is required to be filed, including extensions."),
("Under the centralized partnership audit regime, the person with sole authority to act for the partnership is the:",
 "Partnership representative", ["Tax matters partner", "Managing general partner", "Partner with most capital"],
 "Section 6223 requires a partnership representative, who binds the partnership and all partners in the audit. The tax matters partner belonged to the TEFRA rules that ended for years after 2017."),
("A partnership representative under section 6223 must:",
 "Have substantial U.S. presence", ["Own a partnership interest", "Be a CPA or enrolled agent", "Hold over half the capital"],
 "Section 6223 allows a partner or other person with a substantial presence in the United States to be the partnership representative. That person need not be a partner or a licensed practitioner."),
("A partnership may elect out of the centralized audit regime for 2025 only if it has:",
 "100 or fewer eligible partners", ["100 or fewer partners of any kind", "50 or fewer eligible partners", "10 or fewer individual partners"],
 "An eligible partnership has 100 or fewer partners, all individuals, C corporations, S corporations (counting their shareholders), eligible foreign entities or estates of deceased partners. The election is made each year on Schedule B-2."),
("A partnership has eight partners, one of which is another partnership. For the centralized audit regime it:",
 "Cannot elect out that year", ["May elect out on Schedule B-2", "May elect out with partner consent", "Is out by default under 10 partners"],
 "A partnership is not an eligible partner, so a partnership with a partnership as a partner cannot elect out under section 6221(b), however few partners it has. The old small partnership exception no longer applies."),
("Under the centralized audit regime, an imputed underpayment is generally paid by:",
 "The partnership itself", ["The reviewed-year partners", "The partnership representative", "Partners in the adjustment year"],
 "Section 6225 assesses the imputed underpayment against the partnership in the adjustment year. Partners bear it only through the partnership, unless the partnership elects to push the adjustments out."),
("To push audit adjustments out to its reviewed-year partners, a partnership must elect within:",
 "45 days of the final adjustment", ["30 days of the final adjustment", "90 days of the final adjustment", "60 days of the final adjustment"],
 "Section 6226 requires the push-out election no later than 45 days after the date of the notice of final partnership adjustment. The reviewed-year partners then take the adjustments into account."),
("A partnership's insolvency exclusion for canceled debt income is tested:",
 "At each partner's level", ["At the partnership's level", "At either level by election", "Only by general partners"],
 "Section 108(d)(6) applies the bankruptcy, insolvency and similar exclusions at the partner level. A partner who is solvent includes the share of canceled debt even if the partnership itself is insolvent."),
("Ava sells her partnership interest for $30,000 cash, and the buyer takes over her $12,000 share of partnership liabilities. Her amount realized is:",
 "$42,000", ["$30,000", "$18,000", "$12,000"],
 "Relief from a share of partnership liabilities is treated as money received under section 752(d), so the amount realized is $30,000 + $12,000 = $42,000."),
("Payments to a retiring partner for her share of partnership property are treated under section 736(b) as:",
 "Distributions for her interest", ["Guaranteed payments to her", "Deductions of the partnership", "Her distributive share of income"],
 "Section 736(b) treats liquidating payments made for a retiring or deceased partner's interest in partnership property as distributions. Other payments are a distributive share or guaranteed payments under section 736(a)."),
("For section 751, a partnership's unrealized receivables include its:",
 "Potential section 1245 recapture", ["Notes receivable from partners", "Accounts already collected in cash", "Section 1231 gain on its land"],
 "Section 751(c) treats depreciation recapture the partnership would have on a sale of its assets as an unrealized receivable, alongside rights to payment for goods and services not yet included in income."),
("Under section 708, a partnership terminates for tax purposes when:",
 "No partner carries on any business", ["Half its interests sell in 12 months", "A general partner dies", "A new partner is admitted"],
 "After 2017 a partnership ends only when no part of its business continues to be carried on by any partner in a partnership. The old technical termination on a 50% sale was repealed by the 2017 tax act."),
("When a partner dies, the partnership's tax year:",
 "Closes for that partner", ["Closes for all partners", "Closes for no one", "Ends the partnership"],
 "Section 706(c)(2)(A) closes the year for a partner whose entire interest terminates, by death or otherwise, so the decedent's share up to the date of death goes on the final individual return."),
("A partner contributes a capital asset she held 3 years for a partnership interest. Her holding period for the interest:",
 "Includes the 3 years", ["Starts on the contribution", "Starts when profits begin", "Is short-term for a year"],
 "Under section 1223(1), a partnership interest received for a capital or section 1231 asset in a nontaxable exchange takes the holding period of the property contributed."),
("Partnership capital accounts on 2025 Schedules K-1 must be reported using:",
 "The tax basis method", ["The GAAP book method", "The section 704(b) method", "Any method the partners pick"],
 "The Form 1065 instructions require item L capital accounts to be reported on the tax basis method. A partner's tax capital account can still differ from adjusted basis, which also counts liabilities."),
("Once a partnership makes a section 754 election, it applies:",
 "To later years until revoked", ["Only to the year it is made", "Only to the sale that prompted it", "For a fixed 5 tax years"],
 "A section 754 election covers the year made and all later years, so basis adjustments under sections 734(b) and 743(b) apply to every later distribution and transfer until the IRS consents to revocation."),
]
